# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.net23, REST=1 (with WIFID=1), MORE_JOBS="com.apple.bluetoothd com.apple.BlueTool",
# connsys_step=17 connsys_bt=2, XNU_SECS=130, applog=1 applog_name=Preferences.
#
# Run 90 (logs/lancelot-connsys40.log) brought the missing neighbours: with REST=1 every job of the
# system image is in the small image (started on demand), and
#   accountsd.accountmanager, nehelper, corefollowup.agent -- there
# and bluetoothd (pid 21) with com.apple.server.bluetooth -- there, next to the six HCI commands the
# CONNAC answered (connsys_bt=2). But the tap missed: 0.875 0.71 is empty space. The picture that run
# took (0.543 0.712, see below) has the home screen's fourth row as Health, Wallet, Settings -- three
# icons, not four -- because Maps moved up to the third row (fourth column): with the rest of the
# jobs present the grid differs from the one run 84 tapped.
#
# So the tap is on the icon that is in the picture: Settings, third of the fourth row, 0.543 0.712 of
# the 300x650 panel. "watchdie" says whether it appears and whether (and after how long) it goes, and
# "end" in the same command line stops the run at that death, so the reason applog=1 put on the
# console (run 88: "attempt to insert nil object from objects[3]") survives in the console's tail --
# and if it does not die this time, the tail says "still there", which is the other answer.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 22
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 10
/redwood/bin/net_test fbwait 60
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 16
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.543 0.712
/redwood/bin/net_test watchdie Preferences 30 end